      "side": 1,
      "message": "Captive portals are that, they are INVALID with NET_CAPABILITY_CAPTIVE_PORTAL, unless you intend to have the ConnDiag API translate NetworkMonitor status into this – which I recommend against, because it would be fairly confusing.\n\nWorse : actually NetworkMonitor declares a network valid also if the user said \"use the network as is\" or if validation is skipped (e.g. for VPNs).\n\nThis makes sense for using the network but unfortunately it\u0027s fairly useless for ConnDiags ; maybe we should have a different set of constants to be more useful for this use case.\n\nI should have thought of this earlier \u003c.\u003c\n\n\nThat being said, maybe the detailed constants below for each result are enough. Do check what happens for networks that don\u0027t undergo validation though – I suspect it will tell you VALID with no probe result at all.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 23,
